pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test (wrong verdict): the second face of the `contradiction_proven`
% defect. Under `strengthening_to_core on` a checked deletion becomes a proof by
% contradiction (`DeletionChecker` sets `proof_by_contradiction_subproof` and
% generates no database obligations), so it must show that the deleted
% constraint is implied. `proofgoal 1` used to be answered with a goal invented
% from database constraint 1 and its discharge set `contradiction_proven`, so
% `1 ~x1 >= 1` was deleted for free -- and the formula, which is UNSATISFIABLE
% (`1 x1 >= 1` and `1 ~x1 >= 1` cannot both hold), reported
% `s VERIFIED SATISFIABLE`.
f 2;
strengthening_to_core on;
del id 2 : : subproof
    proofgoal 1
        pol -1 1 +;
    qed;
qed;
sol x1 x2;
output NONE;
conclusion SAT;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
